package database

// balanceFloorNote is the note on the level rows 1-14 of the tuning of
// 2026-10-30 that even out the floor's step: an NPC's least hit is
// (level+1)/2 (defence.go's creatureRoll), a step up at each odd level, and
// at levels 1-14 most of its hits on a tank are that floor; damage_pct there
// is the line's times the floor's line (L/2 + 1/4) over the floor.
const balanceFloorNote = "damage_pct x (2L+1)/(4*ceil(L/2)): the floor's step evened out (tools/tune_balance.py)"

// BalanceSeedLevels and BalanceSeedCons are the rows ensureBalance gives a
// balancelevel or balancecon table it makes (BalanceSeedClasses and
// BalanceSeedClassLevels a balanceclass or balanceclasslevel table): the
// tuning of 2026-10-30 (claude-notes/balance-20261029.md), found with the
// fight simulator (entity/balancesim.go, cmd/balancesim) on eqoaclassic's
// own items, spells and pets, to the user's targets of that day: "Yellow
// (+1/+2): should be a scary fight, at least take you down to less than a
// third hp" and still usually won; "Red (+3 and up): needs a group", a lone
// player's loss and a fitting group of two or three's win. A table made
// before takes them from tools/tune_balance.py and then tools/retune_balance.py
// (the 04:20 data with the roamers), tools/tune_pets.py,
// tools/fit_pet_selfbuffs.py, tools/refit_eqoaemu_balance.py (the re-fit
// once EQOAEmu's workbook is in, 2026-11-01) and its follow-ups' re-fits
// (tools/refit_eqoaemu_followup.py, tools/refit_eqoaemu_followup2.py; each
// logged, --undo), never at an open;
// entity/balancesim_real_test.go holds them to the targets on the real
// kits (EQOA_REAL_DB) and replays the fight the user called "too easy" (a
// level 5 shadow knight of 170 hit points killed a level 6 fire bat in 24 s
// and kept 65%: the simulator's same fight keeps 65% under the tables
// before, 15% under these), entity/balancesim_test.go to the shape.
//
// By level (2026-10-29's, kept): the NPCs' hit points and melee so that a
// player of the level, in the middling gear of its last ten levels and
// fighting as its class plays, beats an even NPC in about 40 seconds (15 at
// level 1) with about two thirds of its hit points left, the middle of ten
// classes (every tank, melee class and priest); the tuning of 2026-10-30
// left an even fight there. Since then con_pct is 100 at every level (it was
// 0 at 1-8, 25 at 10 and 70 at 15, so a low level's yellow was an even NPC
// one level up), and the rows 1-14 even out the floor's step
// (balanceFloorNote: without them a yellow two up was lost at every odd
// player level of 1-10 and won at every even one). A summoned pet's of its
// owner's level: the spells' pets lag their owners (a magician's last of its
// levels is level 47's Ghilan, an enchanter's come every eight to ten
// levels); since the workbook's pets (petstats.go: each a player of its kind,
// with the workbook's weapon, armour and hit points) its columns are 100 at
// every level (below). By con: one and two up 1.47 and 1.4 times the NPC's melee and 68%
// and 70% of the damage dealt it, three up 1.9 and 53%, four 2.2 and 45%,
// five and past 2.3 and 45%: with every class's share by its level
// (BalanceSeedClassLevels) a class's yellow one up ends near 28% of its hit
// points, won four times in five or more, and a red three up is a lone
// player's loss. BalanceSeedClassLevels are the re-fit after EQOAEmu's
// spell workbook went in (2026-11-01, tools/refit_eqoaemu_balance.py; the
// user: "Workbook wins, re-fit"): its spells, effects, masteries and pets in
// the place of ours had moved every class off the targets of 2026-10-30 (the
// tanks and melee classes kept 40-65% through a yellow, the priests won
// their reds alone, the pets every red alone), so each class's rows are
// fitted again on the workbook's books and pets, by the method of the
// tunings before: against SOE's roamers (tools/seed_roamers.py: a Critical
// Hit of 7.4 a level from level 10), its share of an NPC's melee to both
// yellows at once in its own play (by hand; a wizard's and an alchemist's
// root, rooting with a root that holds through a hit, in a kit armed for
// its arts: balancekit.go), its own damage landing more (DealtPct) where no
// share met both yellows' win rates, a healer's share eased 8% off its cliff,
// a red three up made a lone loss by the share times 1.15^k, every
// summoner's pet's hit points (PetHPPct) on the pet its book gives (the
// wizard's familiars are passive: its column 100), and at levels 1-10 every
// class's even fights won about 95% of the time and blue and green ones about
// all of it, by hand and in its own play, in a new character's starting gear
// at 1-5; eleven cells set after (a shadow knight of 5 to the user's fire
// bat fight, a magician of 4 and an alchemist of 6 to the even fights, a
// druid of 5 and 10 and a magician of 44's pet to their reds, five yellows
// the cut left at the edge of their win rates); the shadow knight's 13-60
// fitted with Punish Death for the undead alone (the undead check of
// 2026-11-01). Then fitted again for the import's follow-up fixes
// (tools/refit_eqoaemu_followup.py, the same day): a monk's bare hands roll
// a hand-to-hand DMG and its punches are cast, a ranger dual wields and
// switches to its bow, a paladin's kit switches to a blunt weapon, Avatar
// heals once and no kit wears a NO RENT item or a broken record, so the
// monk's, the ranger's and the paladin's rows 1-60, the bard's 1-13 and 60
// and the shaman's 51-54 are the simulator's fit on them by the same
// method, with cells at the targets' edges set after (a shadow knight of 53
// and 60, a druid of 41 and 53, an enchanter's pet at 52 and 60, an
// alchemist of 16, a rooting wizard of 50 and 60). And again for the
// follow-ups' second round (tools/refit_eqoaemu_followup2.py, the same
// evening): a ranger is back on its blades after an arrow art in melee
// reach, a creature's effects count in its fights (a player's debuffs on
// it), the simulator's player casts its book's pure debuffs and drains in a
// long fight, roots and snares that end at a hit hold until one, the pets'
// abilities are the workbook's, the druid's and the shaman's leftovers are
// out of their lists, the level 60 epic options and the broken records take
// real records, and a backstab needs its caster behind its target, so the
// ranger's rows 8-60, the shaman's 4-60 and its pet's, the rogue's 12-60, the
// shadow knight's 21-51, the warrior's 46-60,
// the bard's 57-60, the druid's 50-60, the enchanter's pet's 5-60 and the
// necromancer's pet's 5-7 and 34-60 are the simulator's fit on them by the
// same method, with cells at the targets' edges set after (a ranger of 10,
// a shadow knight of 24, 28 and 50, a druid of 60, a rogue of 35 for its
// wisps, a bard and a monk of 60,
// the enchanter's pet at 45 and at every level 49-60). A new database wants
// tools/seed_roamers.py too, and the workbook's import and both its
// follow-ups: these rows are fitted on them.
//
// The combat arts' cooldown (art_cooldown_ms, by the player's level): 1.5 s
// at every level, the length a global cooldown commonly has, so no burst
// lands five arts in a second (a level 60 warrior's landed 5,000 in four
// seconds); the simulator found it changes a fight's end little (tanks and
// bards within a few points of hit points left, a monk 3-10 fewer at 45-60,
// a rogue's even fight at 60 13 fewer), and 3 s cost a rogue of 60 its even
// fights' safety (96% won with 24% left).
//
// A summoned pet's hit points and hits (pet_hp_pct, pet_damage_pct): 100 at
// every level since the workbook's pets (2026-11-01): a workbook pet fights
// as a player of its kind, so its hits land as a player's and its hit points
// are the workbook's times its owner's class and level share
// (BalanceSeedClassLevels). 2026-10-30's columns (pet_hp_pct 100 at 1-8 to
// 540 at 60, pet_damage_pct 225-560) were fitted for the server's own pets,
// which hit with a creature's roll: under them a magician's and a
// necromancer's workbook pet won every red alone from 8 with 60-99% left. A
// pet heals a 50 of them every tick (npcregen.go). BalanceSeedRevisions still
// takes a table's rows at the first tuning's (230 ... 800) to 2026-10-29's
// seven tenths of them, which tools/tune_balance.py then takes to 2026-10-30's
// and tools/refit_eqoaemu_balance.py to these.
//
// A creature's heal out of a fight (regen_pct): 5% of its hit points a tick
// from its third tick (the user: "Mobs regen slower"; jib's was 15%), so one
// left empty is whole in about 2 min 10 s, one left at half in 1 min 12 s:
// longer than an even fight (about 40 s) and a red's (70-90 s), so a fight
// broken off and taken up again inside that time is not lost, and still
// shorter than a player's rest (2-3% a tick: 3-5 minutes from empty), so
// no player out-rests a creature to wear it down over pulls.
